  {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"Netty 4.2.7.Final is transitively resolved, but its adaptive allocator can fail under Native Image; no extra dependency or Docker image is needed. ([POM](https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/io/netty/contrib/netty-codec-multipart-core/1.0.0.Final/netty-codec-multipart-core-1.0.0.Final.pom), [Netty issue](https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/15397))\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Set -Dio.netty.allocator.type=unpooled before any Netty class initializes, for both JVM and native-test execution. Exercise PostBodyDecoder.builder() with in-memory Unpooled buffers for multipart and URL-encoded data, following the upstream API documentation. ([Documentation](https://github.com/netty-contrib/codec-multipart))\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"This is a Native Image workaround that bypasses Netty 4.2's adaptive allocator; local Gradle and Native Image verification remains authoritative.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
