te the discovery JSON failed with `bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR: Operation not permitted`. Consequently, no test, metadata, execution-metrics, or dynamic-access coverage files were generated.\n\nPreserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9831-library-new-request-io.netty.contrib-netty-codec-multipart-core-1.0.0.Final-985e6efd\n\nInspect:\n- `logs/io.netty.contrib:netty-codec-multipart-core:1.0.0.Final/discover-artifact-metadata/discover_artifact_metadata.log`\n- `logs/io.netty.contrib:netty-codec-multipart-core:1.0.0.Final/library-preparation-preflight/codex.log`\n- `logs/io.netty.contrib:netty-codec-multipart-core:1.0.0.Final/library-preparation-preflight/codex-session-hanc5ep5.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Correct the Codex/bubblewrap workspace-write configuration and rerun artifact discovery, then confirm the discovery JSON contains the upstream `netty-contrib/codec-multipart` URLs.\n2. Regenerate the library scaffold and tests, setting `io.netty.allocator.type=unpooled` before Netty initialization and exercising multipart and URL-encoded `PostBodyDecoder` flows with in-memory `Unpooled` buffers.\n3. Run the coordinate-scoped metadata validation, JVM tests, and native-image tests, then regenerate metrics and dynamic-access coverage.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_027dbb1d79a56121016a9ee2350b6087d29263a8604edf0412\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 15279, "output": 918, "cacheRead": 111360, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516, "totalTokens": 127557, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1788797474672, "responseId": "resp_027dbb1d79a56121016a9ee2235ec487d29c289d36cdbf6c10", "rawStopReason": "completed"}, "toolResults": []}
